# Line endings
#
# Two people on two operating systems will otherwise produce phantom diffs: git
# stores whatever line endings your machine wrote, so a file saved on Windows
# and then touched on a Mac shows up as *every line changed* even when one word
# moved. Reviewing that is impossible, and it has already happened here - the
# repository arrived from Windows with mixed CRLF and LF in the same file.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises everything to LF inside git, whatever either of
# us is running locally. Set once, never think about it again.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must keep CRLF to work on Windows
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary - never touch, never diff
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary

# Generated - collapse in pull requests so review stays readable.
# These are real files under review, just not ones anyone reads line by line.
package-lock.json    linguist-generated=true
component-catalog.json linguist-generated=true
src/components/Icon/icons/** linguist-generated=true

# SVG is text, but treat it as data rather than code in language stats
*.svg -linguist-detectable
